WEBVTT

1
00:00:33.625 --> 00:00:36.291
In the previous verses, Lord Krishna shed light

2
00:00:36.291 --> 00:00:39.625
on the importance of His
 remembrance at the final moment.

3
00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:41.708
Now in this ninth verse

4
00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.750
of the eighth chapter,

5
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.166
He's describing those divine qualities

6
00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:48.333
on which seekers can meditate.

7
00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:51.750
This guidance is extremely useful
 for devotees on the path of devotion

8
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:55.208
as well as for yoga practitioners.

9
00:00:55.208 --> 00:00:57.416
In the next few verses,

10
00:00:57.416 --> 00:00:59.916
He will further describe these divine qualities.

11
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:07.500
In this verse of the Bhagavad Gita, Lord Krishna

12
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.416
describes His many divine qualities

13
00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:11.541
that help devotees

14
00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:14.625
focus their meditation on Him.

15
00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:15.750
Each quality shows

16
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.750
a specific aspect

17
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:19.958
of His supernatural form.

18
00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:23.541
Kavi, meaning omniscient: Lord Krishna

19
00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:28.250
knows everything – past, present, and future.

20
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.000
His this knowledge isn't limited

21
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.083
like mere human understanding, rather

22
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:36.291
He is the guide of all souls.

23
00:01:36.291 --> 00:01:38.583
Purāṇa, meaning eternal:

24
00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:40.500
Lord Krishna is without beginning

25
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.250
and is the original source of all creation.

26
00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.541
Although He Himself appears timeless

27
00:01:45.541 --> 00:01:48.083
and immortal,

28
00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:51.416
actually He is the beginning of all creation

29
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:55.125
who also sustains it for infinite time.

30
00:01:55.125 --> 00:01:58.333
Anuśāsitāram, meaning supreme controller:

31
00:01:58.333 --> 00:02:00.416
Lord Krishna conducts the universe

32
00:02:00.416 --> 00:02:02.750
and all its activities.

33
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.916
He gives education to mankind

34
00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:07.958
and maintains universal order.

35
00:02:07.958 --> 00:02:10.458
Unlike human controllers, His

36
00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:13.833
guidance arises from divine compassion.

37
00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:17.541
Aņor aņīyam, meaning subtler than the subtlest:

38
00:02:17.541 --> 00:02:19.500
Lord Krishna can enter

39
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.875
even the smallest particle,

40
00:02:20.875 --> 00:02:22.625
even the atom.

41
00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:26.250
Although He is extremely vast,

42
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.416
as paramātmā He's also present

43
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:32.166
within every being,

44
00:02:32.166 --> 00:02:34.625
which displays His nature

45
00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:36.375
beyond imagination.

46
00:02:36.375 --> 00:02:41.000
Sarvasya dhātāram, meaning sustainer of all:

47
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.666
As the world's sustainer, Lord Krishna

48
00:02:43.666 --> 00:02:47.833
provides foundation to every existence –

49
00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:50.666
from the smallest particle to
 the most massive galaxy –

50
00:02:50.666 --> 00:02:53.583
through His divine powers.

51
00:02:53.583 --> 00:02:57.708
Acintya-rūpam, meaning inconceivable form:

52
00:02:57.708 --> 00:02:59.166
Lord Krishna's form

53
00:02:59.166 --> 00:03:02.708
cannot be understood through
 material logic or thought.

54
00:03:02.708 --> 00:03:04.583
He's beyond both the reach of human intellect

55
00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:08.000
and the limits of material nature.

56
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.375
Āditya-varṇam,

57
00:03:09.375 --> 00:03:12.875
meaning radiant like the sun:

58
00:03:12.875 --> 00:03:14.583
Lord Krishna's divine form

59
00:03:14.583 --> 00:03:17.666
is full of the brilliance of countless suns.

60
00:03:17.666 --> 00:03:21.041
This radiance is symbol of His divine presence,

61
00:03:21.041 --> 00:03:25.875
which illuminates Himself
 and everything around Him.

62
00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:28.916
Tamasaḥ parastāt, meaning

63
00:03:28.916 --> 00:03:32.333
beyond māyā: Lord Krishna is divine,

64
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:35.000
beyond the darkness of the material world.

65
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.791
He's unaffected by nature's three guṇas

66
00:03:36.791 --> 00:03:41.250
that is sattva, rajas, and tamas

67
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.750
that keep all beings in bondage.

68
00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.791
Contemplation of these qualities

69
00:03:46.791 --> 00:03:49.791
paves the way to meditate on Lord Krishna,

70
00:03:49.791 --> 00:03:53.166
reveals His personal and divine nature,

71
00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:59.666
and helps devotees develop
 a deep connection with Him.

72
00:04:04.708 --> 00:04:07.916
Have you ever thought

73
00:04:07.916 --> 00:04:10.500
that the essence of spiritual practice

74
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.875
isn't hidden in just worship
 rituals or religious rules,

75
00:04:14.875 --> 00:04:19.750
but in divine relationship?

76
00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.333
When we do spiritual practice,

77
00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:26.333
it's easy to get entangled in 

78
00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:30.583
worship methods and daily routine.

79
00:04:30.583 --> 00:04:34.041
Although these are important,

80
00:04:34.041 --> 00:04:37.375
true devotion begins

81
00:04:37.375 --> 00:04:41.500
when you move beyond just worship rituals.

82
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.416
Think,

83
00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:48.500
how do you remember people in this world?

84
00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.916
Often their kindness, wisdom, or capability –

85
00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:55.583
those special qualities

86
00:04:55.583 --> 00:04:59.125
through which you're attracted to them.

87
00:04:59.125 --> 00:05:01.583
Similarly,

88
00:05:01.583 --> 00:05:05.375
to remember Me,

89
00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:09.208
focus on My divine qualities.

90
00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:14.333
These qualities aren't just 
invisible imaginary thoughts.

91
00:05:14.333 --> 00:05:16.958
Contemplation on these

92
00:05:16.958 --> 00:05:19.708
helps build a personal relationship

93
00:05:19.708 --> 00:05:22.416
between us.

94
00:05:22.416 --> 00:05:24.083
Just as

95
00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:26.416
dry earth

96
00:05:26.416 --> 00:05:29.333
yearns for water,

97
00:05:29.333 --> 00:05:32.541
similarly the soul

98
00:05:32.541 --> 00:05:37.250
remains eager to 

99
00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.916
get drenched in My grace's rain.

100
00:05:38.916 --> 00:05:42.041
By reflecting on My qualities,

101
00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:46.375
you create a simple and clear

102
00:05:46.375 --> 00:05:50.000
path to focus your mind on Me.

103
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.125
You become attracted to Me from the heart.

104
00:05:55.125 --> 00:05:57.625
This is the key to making your meditation

105
00:05:57.625 --> 00:06:03.416
more emotional and natural.

106
00:06:03.416 --> 00:06:08.541
When you see Me not just as a distant deity

107
00:06:08.541 --> 00:06:11.583
but as someone nearest, inspiring,

108
00:06:11.583 --> 00:06:15.500
endowed with these qualities,

109
00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:21.000
then remembering Me will seem easy for you

110
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.291
even amidst life's busyness.

111
00:06:25.291 --> 00:06:28.166
Whether there's peace and happiness

112
00:06:28.166 --> 00:06:33.208
or struggles' fire burns, the mind keeps singing

113
00:06:33.208 --> 00:06:38.083
Hari Hari, always there will be

114
00:06:38.083 --> 00:06:39.708
remembrance!

115
00:06:44.625 --> 00:06:46.916
In family life,

116
00:06:46.916 --> 00:06:49.250
it's natural

117
00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:53.291
that you consider yourself the one who provides

118
00:06:53.291 --> 00:06:57.708
for your loved ones.

119
00:06:57.708 --> 00:07:01.708
Your efforts are important,

120
00:07:01.708 --> 00:07:03.500
but

121
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.416
keep in mind

122
00:07:06.416 --> 00:07:08.541
that I am

123
00:07:08.541 --> 00:07:12.750
the real sustainer –

124
00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:14.541
meaning dhātaram.

125
00:07:14.541 --> 00:07:17.666
I provide not only gross necessities

126
00:07:17.666 --> 00:07:23.625
like food, shelter, and resources,

127
00:07:23.625 --> 00:07:26.333
but also strengthen 

128
00:07:26.333 --> 00:07:33.833
the subtle aspects of love, care,
 and emotionality.

129
00:07:33.833 --> 00:07:35.625
Because

130
00:07:35.625 --> 00:07:38.833
as paramātmā,

131
00:07:38.833 --> 00:07:43.458
I reside in everyone's inner self.

132
00:07:43.458 --> 00:07:46.041
Think,

133
00:07:46.041 --> 00:07:48.875
as a householder,

134
00:07:48.875 --> 00:07:52.250
where does your capability
 come from to take care

135
00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:58.083
of all your home members' needs?

136
00:07:58.083 --> 00:08:01.500
With deep contemplation, you'll experience

137
00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:06.041
that you're playing your role,

138
00:08:06.041 --> 00:08:09.625
but actually I am the one

139
00:08:09.625 --> 00:08:11.375
giving support

140
00:08:11.375 --> 00:08:15.875
to your family.

141
00:08:15.875 --> 00:08:18.000
Every act of compassion,

142
00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.333
every emotional connection that you experience

143
00:08:23.333 --> 00:08:27.291
flows from My divine energy.

144
00:08:27.291 --> 00:08:29.125
Just as

145
00:08:29.125 --> 00:08:34.500
a raining cloud drenches every roof equally

146
00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:37.041
without discrimination,

147
00:08:37.041 --> 00:08:39.000
similarly

148
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.166
My love

149
00:08:40.166 --> 00:08:41.458
reaches every member

150
00:08:41.458 --> 00:08:45.708
of your family.

151
00:08:45.708 --> 00:08:49.166
This understanding can lighten the burden

152
00:08:49.166 --> 00:08:51.625
from your shoulders,

153
00:08:51.625 --> 00:08:54.416
reminding that

154
00:08:54.416 --> 00:09:00.208
you're not alone in this responsibility.

155
00:09:00.208 --> 00:09:01.583
If you recognize

156
00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:05.000
My presence in your family,

157
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.041
you'll experience true joy

158
00:09:07.041 --> 00:09:10.750
and peace.

159
00:09:15.583 --> 00:09:18.416
In your professional life,

160
00:09:18.416 --> 00:09:21.541
when you're leading,

161
00:09:21.541 --> 00:09:23.916
you have to see situations

162
00:09:23.916 --> 00:09:27.041
in two ways –

163
00:09:27.041 --> 00:09:30.250
First, anuśāsitāram,

164
00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:35.208
meaning controller or one
 who enforces discipline.

165
00:09:35.208 --> 00:09:37.708
And second,

166
00:09:37.708 --> 00:09:42.166
dhātaram, meaning one who helps 

167
00:09:42.166 --> 00:09:48.458
with tender mind or provider.

168
00:09:48.458 --> 00:09:50.875
Just as I

169
00:09:50.875 --> 00:09:54.208
conduct the universe with both guidance

170
00:09:54.208 --> 00:09:58.083
and care,

171
00:09:58.083 --> 00:10:01.916
similarly you too must balance

172
00:10:01.916 --> 00:10:08.000
these roles to become an effective leader.

173
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.083
Being a controller means

174
00:10:10.083 --> 00:10:12.625
you set boundaries,

175
00:10:12.625 --> 00:10:14.125
provide direction,

176
00:10:14.125 --> 00:10:19.958
and ensure discipline within your team.

177
00:10:19.958 --> 00:10:21.708
Just as a sailor needs

178
00:10:21.708 --> 00:10:25.250
a compass,

179
00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:32.375
similarly your team needs your clear guidance.

180
00:10:32.375 --> 00:10:37.333
Without this, they can lose 

181
00:10:37.333 --> 00:10:40.416
their goal and purpose.

182
00:10:40.416 --> 00:10:42.375
But listen – leadership

183
00:10:42.375 --> 00:10:47.208
isn't only about control.

184
00:10:47.208 --> 00:10:51.833
You must also become a sustainer

185
00:10:51.833 --> 00:10:55.291
who supports, nourishes,

186
00:10:55.291 --> 00:10:57.958
and provides resources 

187
00:10:57.958 --> 00:11:02.583
for your team's development.

188
00:11:02.583 --> 00:11:04.083
Suppose

189
00:11:04.083 --> 00:11:06.208
your team member

190
00:11:06.208 --> 00:11:09.291
is working on a difficult project

191
00:11:09.291 --> 00:11:12.541
and facing challenges.

192
00:11:12.541 --> 00:11:15.208
Will you only demand results

193
00:11:15.208 --> 00:11:17.333
or also provide help

194
00:11:17.333 --> 00:11:20.541
and guidance?

195
00:11:20.541 --> 00:11:24.000
When you show empathy,

196
00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.708
give cooperation,

197
00:11:25.708 --> 00:11:28.916
and provide appropriate means,

198
00:11:28.916 --> 00:11:32.791
then you create such an environment

199
00:11:32.791 --> 00:11:37.041
where your team truly feels valued

200
00:11:37.041 --> 00:11:41.041
and they're inspired.

201
00:11:41.041 --> 00:11:43.708
Balance of both these aspects

202
00:11:43.708 --> 00:11:48.333
is what makes a leader truly effective.

203
00:11:48.333 --> 00:11:53.375
Just as balance between safety and freedom

204
00:11:53.375 --> 00:11:55.500
is necessary for a child's development,

205
00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:56.958
similarly

206
00:11:56.958 --> 00:12:00.291
balance between control and being supportive

207
00:12:00.291 --> 00:12:04.583
is essential for the workplace.

208
00:12:04.583 --> 00:12:07.833
If you lean too much toward control,

209
00:12:07.833 --> 00:12:10.083
you can become too rigid

210
00:12:10.083 --> 00:12:12.291
and isolated.

211
00:12:12.291 --> 00:12:18.291
If you focus only on nurturing without discipline,

212
00:12:18.291 --> 00:12:21.791
then the team's direction can go astray.

213
00:12:21.791 --> 00:12:25.000
This very balance is the key

214
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:27.750
to successfully lead your team

215
00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:34.416
and inspire them to give their best.

216
00:12:34.416 --> 00:12:39.333
By adopting this confluence of
 discipline and compassion,

217
00:12:39.333 --> 00:12:43.583
you'll become not only a successful leader

218
00:12:43.583 --> 00:12:45.750
but also such a person

219
00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:49.791
whom people follow

220
00:12:49.791 --> 00:12:53.708
with love and respect.
